{"diagnosis": "Fetch test with 256 NOPs (OP-IMM opcode 7'b0010011, e.g. addi x0,x0,0) asserts TRAP and reports FAIL 0xdead with no progress. Current line 877 decodes is_alu_reg_imm as 7'b0010010 instead of 7'b0010011, so OP-IMM is never recognized and with the corrected instr_trap logic every NOP traps. Root cause is the one-bit opcode typo in the mem_do_rinst decoder.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -877,4 +877,4 @@
-			is_alu_reg_imm               <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0010010;
+			is_alu_reg_imm               <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0010011;
 			is_alu_reg_reg               <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0110011;

 			{ decoded_imm_j[31:20], decoded_imm_j[10:1], decoded_imm_j[11], decoded_imm_j[19:12], decoded_imm_j[0] } <= $signed({mem_rdata_latched[31:12], 1'b0});
", "expected": "tohost PASS, TRAP deasserted, checksum != c2a7a4d6295484feeb9ec1ea9381732b8e39a7ccd1997c7d70f6454da2fb4659"}

